WEBVTT

01:41.950 --> 01:49.009
[Genius Girlfriend]

01:49.430 --> 01:51.930
[Episode 5]

02:03.400 --> 02:04.560
I told myself,

02:07.140 --> 02:08.600
it's great to have a rival.

02:09.360 --> 02:11.820
Whether I win or lose,
all is fair and square.

02:13.000 --> 02:14.900
But another voice in my heart

02:15.530 --> 02:16.630
keeps asking.

02:18.870 --> 02:21.600
It was you who held my hand
to escape the aquarium.

02:22.710 --> 02:24.970
It was you who buried
the wish box with me.

02:28.430 --> 02:29.860
If this isn't a friend,

02:31.500 --> 02:33.360
then what should a friend be like?

03:00.410 --> 03:00.960
Hey—

03:05.180 --> 03:05.840
Lin Zhixia!

03:06.310 --> 03:07.970
Why are you so absent-minded?

03:11.870 --> 03:12.960
What's wrong?

03:13.560 --> 03:14.840
The only person in our group
who can't have any problems

03:14.840 --> 03:15.740
is you.

03:16.300 --> 03:17.710
Otherwise, as someone
tagging along for the contest,

03:17.710 --> 03:19.770
I won't be able to explain it to my mom.

03:27.190 --> 03:27.690
I...

03:30.150 --> 03:31.520
I have a friend.

03:33.590 --> 03:35.120
Don't say "friend." I know.

03:35.190 --> 03:36.190
Just say it's you.

03:36.590 --> 03:37.850
I really have a friend.

03:41.680 --> 03:43.079
He's quite nice to me,

03:43.560 --> 03:45.960
and I've always treated him
as a good friend.

03:45.960 --> 03:47.560
But recently I heard them say

03:49.590 --> 03:50.800
that they only sees me as a rival

03:50.800 --> 03:52.060
and wants to defeat me.

03:53.410 --> 03:55.000
I've seen plenty of girls like this.

03:55.000 --> 03:56.260
Don't take it to heart.

03:57.560 --> 03:58.560
He's a boy.

03:59.870 --> 04:01.470
A boy is acting like that too?

04:05.080 --> 04:07.410
Lin Zhixia, I didn't know you well before.

04:07.630 --> 04:08.630
I thought you

04:08.650 --> 04:11.080
disdained hanging out
with us ordinary people.

04:11.080 --> 04:12.360
But in this period of time,

04:12.360 --> 04:14.290
I felt you're actually quite nice.

04:14.370 --> 04:17.170
You just aren't good at
getting along with people.

04:17.720 --> 04:19.110
Listen to me.

04:19.829 --> 04:22.160
This friend is definitely jealous of you.

04:22.430 --> 04:23.760
He treats me quite well.

04:25.430 --> 04:26.270
Then...

04:28.560 --> 04:30.070
did he ask you to tutor him

04:30.570 --> 04:32.110
or ask what books you read

04:32.110 --> 04:34.040
and what practice questions you do?

04:34.040 --> 04:35.330
See, he's just using you.

04:35.330 --> 04:36.920
That's why he treats you well.

04:36.920 --> 04:37.830
Listen to me.

04:37.830 --> 04:39.490
I'm very experienced in this.

04:40.240 --> 04:41.120
But...

04:41.140 --> 04:42.409
Fine,

04:43.060 --> 04:43.800
if you don't believe me,

04:43.800 --> 04:45.200
don't you believe books?

04:45.370 --> 04:47.360
I remember a good quote from a book.

04:47.510 --> 04:49.630
Time will filter out fake friends.

04:49.830 --> 04:50.480
This friend of yours

04:50.480 --> 04:52.190
is a fake friend filtered out by time.

04:52.190 --> 04:53.120
Just ignore him.

04:55.600 --> 04:58.130
Then I should just
give him the cold shoulder?

04:59.190 --> 05:01.000
Time will give you the answer.

05:07.950 --> 05:08.920
It's about time.

05:08.920 --> 05:10.320
Let's go back and review.

05:11.870 --> 05:13.670
I thought we were done for today.

05:50.000 --> 05:52.360
Okay, let's do some practice.

05:51.990 --> 05:54.640
[Constantly Strive to Become Stronger;
Strive to Be Number One]

05:52.560 --> 05:53.600
Now, open your book.

05:53.600 --> 05:55.310
Turn to page 27.

05:58.770 --> 05:59.700
Comprehending:

05:59.800 --> 06:00.310
one.

06:00.930 --> 06:02.300
Read the passage carefully

06:02.300 --> 06:04.980
and join the correct part
of the sentences.

06:28.450 --> 06:29.330
Lin Zhixia.

06:31.500 --> 06:33.500
You caused me to miss the contest.

06:34.420 --> 06:37.220
But you prepared
quite well yourself, didn't you?

06:39.130 --> 06:40.260
Wh-What do you want?

06:40.930 --> 06:41.810
Nothing.

06:42.570 --> 06:44.220
I'm free now anyway.

06:44.700 --> 06:45.980
I have plenty of time.

06:54.370 --> 06:55.980
You don't think you can just stick up

06:55.980 --> 06:57.100
for Duan Qiyan

06:57.310 --> 06:58.770
and then walk away, do you?

07:00.770 --> 07:01.830
What are you doing?

07:06.570 --> 07:08.540
If I see you approach Lin Zhixia again,

07:08.540 --> 07:11.180
it won't be as simple as
withdrawing from the contest.

07:11.180 --> 07:12.640
Do you want to be expelled?

07:15.660 --> 07:16.450
Lin Zhixia,

07:17.740 --> 07:19.330
I'll say it right here.

07:20.180 --> 07:20.860
Tomorrow,

07:21.750 --> 07:25.210
don't even think about
participating in the contest in peace.

07:26.070 --> 07:27.330
Let's wait and see.

07:34.930 --> 07:35.740
Are you okay?

08:00.330 --> 08:01.130
Zeqiu,

08:01.810 --> 08:03.870
I want to talk to you about something.

08:07.420 --> 08:08.300
Can you...

08:08.300 --> 08:09.570
No.

08:11.770 --> 08:13.100
I'm trying to say—can you

08:13.100 --> 08:14.760
go to school with me tomorrow?

08:15.930 --> 08:16.920
Did I tell you that at school,

08:16.920 --> 08:18.330
you're not allowed to mention
that you're my sister?

08:18.330 --> 08:19.620
You did, but...

08:19.620 --> 08:20.620
Since you're not my sister,

08:20.620 --> 08:21.860
how can I accompany you to school?

08:21.860 --> 08:23.790
It will cause misunderstandings.

08:25.570 --> 08:27.370
Just for tomorrow, please?

08:28.740 --> 08:29.660
Just one day.

08:33.270 --> 08:34.530
Did something happen?

08:36.510 --> 08:37.030
No.

08:37.620 --> 08:38.150
Nothing.

08:44.720 --> 08:46.320
Keep a distance of 10 meters.

08:47.000 --> 08:47.580
What?

08:48.860 --> 08:50.510
I mean,
when we go to school together tomorrow,

08:50.510 --> 08:52.110
keep a distance of 10 meters.

08:52.650 --> 08:53.580
Don't talk to me,

08:53.630 --> 08:54.770
and no eye contact.

08:54.940 --> 08:56.800
Don't let others misunderstand.

08:57.580 --> 08:59.380
And when we enter the door later,

08:59.860 --> 09:01.390
you only enter when I say so.

09:02.340 --> 09:03.100
Okay.

09:05.250 --> 09:06.310
Good night, Zeqiu.

09:06.410 --> 09:07.070
Good night.

10:40.770 --> 10:41.770
Two more minutes.

10:41.860 --> 10:42.770
If time is up

10:42.770 --> 10:44.030
and your team isn't all here,

10:44.030 --> 10:44.890
you can't participate.

10:44.380 --> 10:48.630
[Nanhai Province Star of Hope Math Contest
Preliminary Round]

10:51.290 --> 10:52.490
Where is Jiang Yubai?

10:53.250 --> 10:54.380
I don't know either.

11:22.650 --> 11:25.520
[Nanhai Province Star of Hope Math Contest
Preliminary Round]

11:33.340 --> 11:33.980
I'm here!

11:34.960 --> 11:35.610
[Nanhai Province Star of Hope Math Contest
Preliminary Round]

11:38.620 --> 11:39.250
Sit down.

11:42.860 --> 11:45.730
[Nanhai Province Star of Hope Math Contest
Preliminary Round]

11:53.470 --> 11:55.470
[Nanhai Province Star of Hope Math Contest
Preliminary Round]

12:09.860 --> 12:11.650
The test is out of 100 points.

12:11.860 --> 12:13.500
You have 120 minutes.

12:14.100 --> 12:15.740
You may begin now.

12:15.470 --> 12:16.950
[Nanhai Province Star of Hope Math Contest
Preliminary Round]

12:24.250 --> 12:26.760
[Nanhai Province Star of Hope Math Contest
Preliminary Round]

12:48.430 --> 12:49.930
[Nanhai Province Star of Hope Math Contest
Preliminary Round]

12:53.360 --> 12:54.750
[Nanhai Province Star of Hope Math Contest
Preliminary Round]

13:28.860 --> 13:29.650
Lin Zhixia,

13:31.170 --> 13:32.410
that multiple-choice question,

13:32.410 --> 13:33.340
the last one,

13:33.840 --> 13:34.910
where xy > 0

13:35.170 --> 13:36.770
and x+y = 1,

13:36.770 --> 13:37.700
do you remember?

13:39.410 --> 13:40.740
Is the answer C?

13:41.050 --> 13:41.460
A.

13:42.650 --> 13:45.250
By introducing auxiliary variables through
variable relationship transformations

13:45.250 --> 13:46.740
and then applying
the Cauchy-Schwarz inequality,

13:46.740 --> 13:48.870
the minimum value
can be solved as 1/3.

13:52.250 --> 13:55.770
We talked about a similar question
in the library the day before yesterday.

13:55.770 --> 13:57.130
I'm doomed.

14:00.960 --> 14:02.820
I saw you sleep for 15 minutes
in the second half.

14:02.820 --> 14:04.950
You completed it so quickly this time.

14:04.980 --> 14:06.240
Speed doesn't matter.

14:06.340 --> 14:07.170
The last question

14:07.170 --> 14:08.890
was obviously out of my league.

14:08.890 --> 14:10.050
If you ask a dog

14:10.250 --> 14:11.820
to answer a Chinese test question,

14:11.820 --> 14:13.010
could it answer it?

14:13.100 --> 14:14.050
That's how I felt.

14:14.050 --> 14:15.510
You seem quite proud of it.

14:15.700 --> 14:17.070
I might not get first place,

14:17.070 --> 14:19.400
but I definitely won't drag our team down.

14:21.340 --> 14:24.540
I told you that you shouldn't have
chosen me as a teammate.

14:25.940 --> 14:26.940
Ms. Last In Class.

14:27.370 --> 14:28.700
How did you do this time?

14:29.370 --> 14:30.900
It's none of your business.

14:31.290 --> 14:32.100
Ignore him.

14:33.620 --> 14:36.050
Let's go. Let's find a place
to help you estimate your score.

14:36.050 --> 14:36.860
The library?

14:37.770 --> 14:38.980
The library again?

14:38.980 --> 14:40.130
I'm hungry.

14:41.500 --> 14:42.430
We can eat first.

14:42.940 --> 14:43.740
Let's go.

14:44.740 --> 14:45.530
Lin Zhixia.

14:48.500 --> 14:49.290
Don't worry.

14:49.820 --> 14:51.750
Your team will definitely make it.

14:53.530 --> 14:55.530
I'll compete with you in the finals.

14:57.220 --> 14:58.020
Rest assured.

14:58.250 --> 14:59.050
This time,

14:59.500 --> 15:01.560
I'll let you know me more completely.

15:09.980 --> 15:10.740
I'm doomed.

15:10.980 --> 15:13.180
I can't even remember if I wrote my name.

15:17.770 --> 15:18.860
Even if I did,

15:18.860 --> 15:20.890
I definitely did terribly on this test.

15:20.890 --> 15:22.220
I might not even pass.

15:29.940 --> 15:31.740
Why did you lose confidence too?

15:33.250 --> 15:36.010
I just talked big to Jiang Yubai.

15:37.130 --> 15:38.740
If we don't make it to the finals,

15:38.740 --> 15:40.220
won't it be super awkward?

15:40.290 --> 15:41.820
What did you just say to him?

15:42.010 --> 15:44.370
"I'll let you know me more completely."

15:44.770 --> 15:45.580
I think

15:46.530 --> 15:48.460
it was even more arrogant than that.

15:48.460 --> 15:50.050
I also told him before

15:50.860 --> 15:52.590
that until the finals are over,

15:52.820 --> 15:54.530
I'd unfriend him

15:54.940 --> 15:56.800
for this to be a pure competition.

15:57.940 --> 15:59.290
You really hyped it up.

16:02.890 --> 16:03.890
Sorry, sorry.

16:04.370 --> 16:05.290
It's all my fault.

16:05.290 --> 16:06.690
This is so embarrassing.

16:14.910 --> 16:16.530
Anyway, the exam is over.

16:16.820 --> 16:18.130
Whether we make it or not,

16:18.130 --> 16:19.720
the result can't be changed.

16:19.720 --> 16:21.690
Let's just have a happy dinner tonight.

16:21.690 --> 16:22.820
Don't overthink it.

16:23.100 --> 16:23.890
My treat.

16:27.700 --> 16:28.900
Screwing up the exam,

16:29.170 --> 16:30.770
even the skewers don't taste good anymore.

16:30.770 --> 16:32.570
Who said you screwed up the exam?

16:32.890 --> 16:35.370
You can't keep giving yourself
this kind of psychological suggestion.

16:35.370 --> 16:37.230
Do you know the Law of Attraction?

16:37.820 --> 16:38.700
What's that?

16:39.250 --> 16:40.910
It's a psychological effect.

16:41.130 --> 16:42.700
If you always think about bad things,

16:42.700 --> 16:44.530
your life will be full of crises.

16:44.890 --> 16:47.410
If you always focus on the good things,

16:47.580 --> 16:49.240
you'll attract good results.

16:50.010 --> 16:50.890
How?

16:51.130 --> 16:53.660
Your thoughts and emotions
emit a frequency.

16:53.700 --> 16:54.620
This frequency

16:54.620 --> 16:57.410
can attract things
with the same frequency in the universe.

16:57.410 --> 17:00.010
So you have to
place an order with the universe.

17:01.050 --> 17:02.250
That sounds amazing.

17:02.770 --> 17:04.420
All right, let's place an order now.

17:03.690 --> 17:04.579
[Three-Two Kitchen]

17:04.640 --> 17:05.099
Come on.

17:06.609 --> 17:07.069
Come on.

17:11.260 --> 17:13.900
We will definitely
do very well in the exam this time,

17:13.900 --> 17:15.290
and we will definitely advance.

17:15.290 --> 17:17.810
We will definitely
do very well in the exam this time,

17:17.810 --> 17:19.050
and we will definitely advance.

17:18.540 --> 17:19.880
[Three-Two Kitchen]

17:19.140 --> 17:22.400
Tang Tingting definitely
wrote her name on the test paper.

17:22.849 --> 17:26.089
Tang Tingting definitely
wrote her name on the test paper.

17:26.089 --> 17:27.900
Then I hope my two friends

17:27.900 --> 17:28.900
won't be so depressed tonight,

17:28.900 --> 17:30.960
and we can have a happy meal together.

17:31.380 --> 17:33.010
It seems to really work.

17:33.050 --> 17:35.330
I feel quite happy now.

17:34.080 --> 17:36.190
[Three-Two Kitchen]

17:37.940 --> 17:39.570
Do you guys feel

17:40.290 --> 17:42.660
like we used to be just teammates,

17:43.050 --> 17:45.110
but now we're more like good friends?

17:46.530 --> 17:48.610
Actually, in a way,

17:48.850 --> 17:50.660
teammates have a deeper bond than friends.

17:50.660 --> 17:53.700
After all, we have to experience success,
failure, joy, and sorrow together.

17:53.700 --> 17:56.660
Working together
forces you to adapt to each other

17:56.660 --> 17:58.190
and understand each other.

17:58.460 --> 17:59.460
In difficult times,

17:59.460 --> 18:01.720
we will understand and trust each other.

18:02.530 --> 18:04.270
So since we are teammates,

18:04.900 --> 18:06.360
we are naturally friends.

18:08.850 --> 18:09.910
Let's make a toast.

18:11.090 --> 18:13.180
We will definitely
do very well in the exam this time,

18:13.180 --> 18:14.220
and we will definitely advance.

18:14.220 --> 18:14.950
Definitely!

18:15.010 --> 18:15.980
Cheers!

18:17.730 --> 18:21.550
[Three-Two Kitchen]

18:21.840 --> 18:23.790
[School notice board]

18:24.660 --> 18:25.830
Lin Zhixia, look for it quickly.

18:25.830 --> 18:26.960
I don't dare to look.

18:27.350 --> 18:29.200
[Announcement of the Finalists]

18:28.290 --> 18:28.820
Let's go.

18:33.100 --> 18:35.420
What's wrong? Did we not make it?

18:37.500 --> 18:38.100
We made it.

18:38.750 --> 18:39.550
Fourth place.

18:40.570 --> 18:41.300
Who is first?

18:42.090 --> 18:43.940
A team from the experimental school.

18:43.940 --> 18:45.850
They won because of their average score.

18:45.850 --> 18:47.580
What about Jiang Yubai's team?

18:49.660 --> 18:51.120
You're thinking about us?

18:51.570 --> 18:52.970
We are not that talented—

18:53.420 --> 18:55.830
just the runner-up in the preliminaries.

19:00.010 --> 19:01.070
Congratulations.

19:01.330 --> 19:02.810
You've taken the lead.

19:03.460 --> 19:05.720
Although our team is ranked a bit higher,

19:05.880 --> 19:08.570
you are the only one
with a perfect score in the preliminaries.

19:08.570 --> 19:09.900
There are still finals.

19:11.330 --> 19:11.900
Yeah.

19:12.190 --> 19:13.190
There are finals.

19:14.510 --> 19:15.240
Let's go.

19:16.110 --> 19:17.200
We really made it to the finals.

19:17.200 --> 19:18.200
We really made it.

19:25.070 --> 19:26.400
Why am I smiling?

19:27.720 --> 19:28.590
Happy for her?

19:30.720 --> 19:31.510
Mocking.

19:32.590 --> 19:33.790
I must be mocking her.

19:41.680 --> 19:42.480
Lin Zhixia,

19:42.790 --> 19:45.160
don't think I'm scared
just because someone got your back.

19:45.160 --> 19:46.560
Tell that kid Jiang Yubai

19:46.680 --> 19:47.920
not to be too arrogant.

19:47.920 --> 19:49.050
I will get back at him

19:49.200 --> 19:50.720
sooner or later.

20:14.890 --> 20:16.970
[A New Chapter, A New Journey]

20:18.570 --> 20:23.580
[A New Chapter, A New Journey]

20:45.990 --> 20:50.320
[Weiming Gymnasium]

20:51.630 --> 20:52.970
[Nanhai Province
Star of Hope Math Contest] [Finals]

21:05.550 --> 21:06.780
What should I do? I'm so nervous.

21:06.780 --> 21:09.510
[Nanhai Province
Star of Hope Math Contest] [Finals]

21:07.440 --> 21:09.900
What if I drag down
your average score again?

21:10.510 --> 21:11.790
The finals have a different format.

21:11.790 --> 21:14.160
It's not just
about individual performance.

21:14.160 --> 21:15.590
As long as we cooperate well,

21:15.590 --> 21:16.400
we'll be fine.

21:18.790 --> 21:19.550
What if...

21:19.550 --> 21:20.830
I'm here, don't worry.

21:30.550 --> 21:31.160
Tingting.

21:35.550 --> 21:36.680
Why is my mom here?

21:41.160 --> 21:42.550
Mom, why are you here?

21:42.550 --> 21:44.110
The other students' parents aren't here.

21:44.110 --> 21:45.310
I don't care about others.

21:45.310 --> 21:47.110
I have to come
to my daughter's competition.

21:47.110 --> 21:47.790
Good luck.

21:48.070 --> 21:49.000
Do your best.

21:49.270 --> 21:50.830
All right, go up and have a seat.

21:50.830 --> 21:51.830
Don't get distracted.

21:51.830 --> 21:53.070
I believe in you.

21:53.440 --> 21:54.240
Good luck.

21:54.640 --> 21:55.240
Good luck!

21:57.720 --> 21:59.440
My mom is seriously...

22:00.200 --> 22:01.860
Your mom came to cheer for you.

22:08.070 --> 22:08.640
Ma'am.

22:09.920 --> 22:11.250
Good girl, you're here.

22:11.440 --> 22:12.590
Cheer for her.

22:12.590 --> 22:13.790
Go! She will win!

22:15.160 --> 22:16.480
Why are there parents here?

22:16.480 --> 22:18.810
They didn't ask parents to come, did they?

22:21.110 --> 22:21.920
Come on.

22:22.270 --> 22:23.960
The experimental school team,
who came first in the preliminaries,

22:23.960 --> 22:25.350
is quite strong this year.

22:25.350 --> 22:27.080
I don't know if we have a chance.

22:27.200 --> 22:28.200
Probably?

22:28.350 --> 22:31.110
They say there's
a really amazing student in Grade 10.

22:31.110 --> 22:32.680
She was the top scorer
in the city's high school entrance exam.

22:32.680 --> 22:34.310
I know. It's that girl.

22:34.680 --> 22:36.440
Lin Zhixia, right?

22:35.460 --> 22:36.990
[Nanhai Province
Star of Hope Math Contest] [Finals]

22:36.510 --> 22:39.440
No way. Her team's preliminary performance
was average.

22:39.440 --> 22:40.640
They only came 4th.

22:41.270 --> 22:43.070
I don't have high hopes
for her with this format.

22:43.070 --> 22:44.720
Why do you two have so much to say?

22:44.720 --> 22:46.120
Which class are you from?

22:51.160 --> 22:51.960
Ma'am.

22:52.590 --> 22:54.310
Please turn off the flash.

22:55.510 --> 22:57.070
Just 2 more pictures.

23:01.960 --> 23:03.350
Please rise.

23:04.410 --> 23:07.380
[Nanhai Province
Star of Hope Math Contest] [Finals]

23:05.790 --> 23:07.750
Let's welcome the judges

23:07.470 --> 23:10.030
[Host]

23:07.750 --> 23:09.590
with our warmest applause.

23:21.680 --> 23:29.440
[Nanhai Province
Star of Hope Math Contest] [Finals]

23:22.350 --> 23:23.590
Please take a seat.

23:26.510 --> 23:29.350
Next, I will read the rules
of the competition.

23:29.550 --> 23:33.940
[Nanhai Province
Star of Hope Math Contest rules]

23:29.640 --> 23:31.830
The competition lasts about 300 minutes

23:31.830 --> 23:34.110
and consists of 3 rounds

23:34.110 --> 23:35.680
with increasing difficulty,

23:35.680 --> 23:37.880
testing the mathematical literacy

23:37.880 --> 23:39.340
and teamwork of the contestants.

23:39.340 --> 23:42.100
[Host]

23:39.350 --> 23:41.070
The 1st round is compulsory.

23:41.270 --> 23:42.240
The 3 members of each team, A, B, and C,

23:42.220 --> 23:44.890
[Nanhai Province
Star of Hope Math Contest rules]

23:42.240 --> 23:46.000
will take turns to answer.

23:46.000 --> 23:47.680
Ten points will be added
for a correct answer,

23:47.680 --> 23:49.510
and no points will be deducted
for a wrong one.

23:49.510 --> 23:51.240
The 2nd round is a buzzer round.

23:49.860 --> 23:53.710
[Nanhai Province
Star of Hope Math Contest rules]

23:51.270 --> 23:53.830
Eight teams will compete for 10 questions.

23:54.030 --> 23:55.680
5 points will be added
for a correct answer,

23:55.680 --> 23:57.550
and 5 points will be deducted
for a wrong one.

23:57.550 --> 24:00.480
The 3rd round
is a 60-minute group modeling.

23:59.390 --> 24:03.420
[Nanhai Province
Star of Hope Math Contest rules]

24:00.680 --> 24:01.720
Each team will complete

24:01.720 --> 24:04.750
a comprehensive question
with 3 sub-questions.

24:03.540 --> 24:07.510
[Nanhai Province
Star of Hope Math Contest] [Finals]

24:05.000 --> 24:06.720
The score is 30 points.

24:06.960 --> 24:10.680
Now, the competition begins.

24:07.590 --> 24:10.570
[Host]

24:24.510 --> 24:26.240
Don't be nervous. You can do it.

24:35.370 --> 24:38.500
[Nanhai Province
Star of Hope Math Contest]

24:38.620 --> 24:39.380
[Host]

24:49.120 --> 24:50.220
[Host]

24:52.130 --> 24:53.360
[Nanhai No.1 High School Team 2,
10 points]

25:00.480 --> 25:01.850
[Nanhai No.1 High School Team 4,
10 points]

25:13.790 --> 25:14.790
[Nanhai No.1 High School Team 2,
30 points]

25:14.790 --> 25:15.690
[Nanhai No.1 High School Team 4,
20 points]

25:32.560 --> 25:35.680
[Nanhai No.1 High School Team 2,
50 points]

25:35.790 --> 25:38.200
[Host]

25:36.110 --> 25:36.920
Next,

25:36.920 --> 25:38.520
Contestant No. 3 from Team 4.

25:41.270 --> 25:42.790
Given that parabola C:

25:42.790 --> 25:44.720
y^2 = 4x

25:44.720 --> 25:47.000
has two distinct points A and B

25:45.760 --> 25:48.890
[Nanhai Province
Star of Hope Math Contest]

25:47.200 --> 25:49.070
(A != B)

25:49.270 --> 25:50.720
that are symmetric
with respect to the line l:

25:50.720 --> 25:52.720
y = x + b,

25:52.790 --> 25:55.480
find the range of values
for the real number b.

25:55.590 --> 25:56.480
Please answer.

26:03.400 --> 26:05.260
Why is her question so difficult?

26:17.880 --> 26:19.270
b > -3.

26:19.880 --> 26:21.720
b > -3.

26:21.880 --> 26:23.400
The answer is wrong.

26:24.550 --> 26:27.240
The correct answer is b < -3.

26:28.510 --> 26:29.750
This question is too difficult.

26:29.750 --> 26:30.720
No one could've answered it.

26:30.720 --> 26:31.310
Yeah.

26:31.310 --> 26:32.250
You can't make mistakes

26:32.250 --> 26:33.290
at such a crucial moment.

26:33.040 --> 26:34.880
[Tang Tingting] [Wrong answer]

26:43.180 --> 26:44.160
It's fine.

26:44.480 --> 26:45.700
This question is hard.

26:45.700 --> 26:47.430
We still have the buzzer round.

26:55.000 --> 26:56.830
Now it's the buzzer round.

26:57.000 --> 26:59.030
You can press the buzzer
after the question is read,

26:59.030 --> 27:01.640
but each team only has 1 chance.

27:01.750 --> 27:03.550
Five points will be added
for a correct answer,

27:03.550 --> 27:05.590
and 5 points will be deducted
for a wrong one.

27:05.590 --> 27:07.860
The remaining teams
can continue to buzz in

27:07.860 --> 27:12.400
[Nanhai Province
Star of Hope Math Contest]

27:07.880 --> 27:08.960
until the correct answer is given,

27:08.960 --> 27:11.960
or all teams have used their chances.

27:12.790 --> 27:13.590
Question one.

27:13.720 --> 27:15.550
Two people take turns rolling dice.

27:15.550 --> 27:17.680
Each person rolls 2 dice at a time.

27:17.680 --> 27:19.720
The first to get a sum

27:19.720 --> 27:21.270
greater than 6 wins.

27:21.400 --> 27:23.400
Otherwise, the other person rolls.

27:23.590 --> 27:25.750
What is the winning probability
of the first roller?

27:25.750 --> 27:26.610
Please answer.

27:28.310 --> 27:29.680
Player 1 from team 4.

27:31.960 --> 27:33.200
12/17.

27:33.440 --> 27:34.750
That is correct.

27:37.640 --> 27:38.480
Wow.

27:39.240 --> 27:40.240
That's amazing.

27:45.070 --> 27:46.030
Question two.

27:46.160 --> 27:47.550
Find the range of the function f(x)

27:47.550 --> 27:49.590
which equals squareroot (x - 5)

27:49.590 --> 27:53.000
minutes the squareroot of (24 - 3x).

27:53.000 --> 27:53.860
Please answer.

27:54.640 --> 27:56.510
Player 1 from team 4 again.

27:56.510 --> 27:57.370
Please answer.

28:05.550 --> 28:06.960
Please pay attention
to the time left for answering.

28:06.960 --> 28:08.160
There are 5 seconds left.

28:08.160 --> 28:08.790
Five.

28:09.510 --> 28:10.110
Four.

28:10.720 --> 28:11.400
Three.

28:12.200 --> 28:12.830
Two.

28:13.030 --> 28:14.510
Negative 3 to the square root of 3.

28:14.510 --> 28:16.030
That is correct.

28:17.980 --> 28:19.430
[Nanhai Province
Star of Hope Math Contest]

28:21.640 --> 28:23.270
Lin Zhixia is so amazing.

28:23.440 --> 28:24.880
She didn't even use scratch paper.

28:24.880 --> 28:26.750
She calculated the answer mentally.

28:26.750 --> 28:28.610
My goodness, that's impressive.

28:38.200 --> 28:39.800
How can we compete with that?

28:41.240 --> 28:42.100
There's no way.

28:42.310 --> 28:43.960
Points are deducted for wrong answers.

28:43.960 --> 28:45.160
So before buzzing in,

28:45.310 --> 28:47.240
everyone must be absolutely sure.

28:47.440 --> 28:49.770
But Lin Zhixia doesn't have this concern.

28:49.790 --> 28:51.320
She always buzzes in first,

28:51.350 --> 28:53.680
and calculates after getting the chance.

28:54.030 --> 28:55.290
She's that confident?

28:55.510 --> 28:56.720
Isn't she worried at all

28:56.720 --> 28:59.320
that there might be
a question she can't solve?

29:00.640 --> 29:01.440
No.

29:02.000 --> 29:04.030
We're at a huge disadvantage
if this continues.

29:04.030 --> 29:05.610
If we fall behind in the buzzer round,

29:05.610 --> 29:07.410
we will be very passive later on.

29:07.680 --> 29:09.480
We need to figure something out.

29:12.750 --> 29:13.720
Question 3.

29:13.750 --> 29:15.790
In a 3x3 grid,

29:15.790 --> 29:18.350
going from the top left corner
to the bottom right corner,

29:18.350 --> 29:21.240
you can only move right or down each time.

29:21.480 --> 29:22.110
Find—

29:24.680 --> 29:26.750
Player 1 from team 2, are you sure

29:26.750 --> 29:28.480
you want to answer before the question

29:28.480 --> 29:29.160
is finished?

29:29.160 --> 29:30.350
The question isn't even finished.

29:30.350 --> 29:31.350
That's too hasty.

29:34.110 --> 29:34.830
Yes.

29:35.830 --> 29:37.030
Okay, please answer.

29:40.880 --> 29:41.750
This question

29:42.480 --> 29:44.680
should be asking for the shortest path.

29:47.400 --> 29:48.200
It's 6.

29:48.920 --> 29:51.050
There are 6 different shortest paths.

29:54.000 --> 29:55.060
Team 2's answer...

29:57.270 --> 29:58.160
is correct.

29:58.310 --> 29:58.790
Yes!

30:06.640 --> 30:09.370
Not bad, you've learned
to predict the question.

30:09.830 --> 30:12.030
It's the only way to beat her
to the buzzer.

30:12.030 --> 30:14.490
The following questions
won't be this easy.

30:14.590 --> 30:16.720
If they dare to buzz in like that again,

30:16.790 --> 30:18.250
they'll just lose points.

30:19.680 --> 30:21.510
The difficulty should be increasing
from now on.

30:21.510 --> 30:22.310
Even Lin Zhixia

30:22.310 --> 30:24.000
won't be able
to rely solely on mental math.

30:24.000 --> 30:25.530
We can't let our guard down.

30:27.400 --> 30:29.790
Given that the function y equals a times

30:29.790 --> 30:31.510
cosine squared x minus 3,

30:31.510 --> 30:34.350
times sine x, its minimum value is

30:32.940 --> 30:35.340
[Nanhai Province
Star of Hope Math Contest]

30:44.120 --> 30:45.380
[Nanhai Province Star of Hope
Math Contest] [Correct answer]

31:02.660 --> 31:06.420
[Nanhai Province
Star of Hope Math Contest]

31:05.640 --> 31:08.720
All right,
this is the last buzzer question.

31:09.200 --> 31:13.030
The number of positive integer solutions
to the equation x+y+z=2010,

31:13.030 --> 31:15.200
satisfying x is less than or equal to y,

31:15.200 --> 31:18.160
which is less than or equal to z, is?

31:19.160 --> 31:21.480
Contestant 2 of Team 2, please answer.

31:24.000 --> 31:25.720
The answer is 336843.

31:25.880 --> 31:27.070
Incorrect.

31:27.070 --> 31:28.790
You may now buzz in again.

31:30.590 --> 31:31.960
Contestant 1 of Team 4,

31:31.960 --> 31:33.200
what is your answer?

31:34.510 --> 31:35.790
336675.

31:36.270 --> 31:37.750
Correct.

31:46.100 --> 31:47.600
[Nanhai Province
Star of Hope Math Contest]

31:47.630 --> 31:48.580
[1st Place:
Nanhai No.1 High School, Team 4]

31:48.030 --> 31:50.680
Next, I will announce
the modeling question.

31:48.580 --> 31:49.380
[2nd Place:
Nanhai No.1 High School, Team 2]

31:50.880 --> 31:52.550
In major sports events,

31:52.550 --> 31:55.160
if an athlete successfully breaks
a world record,

31:55.160 --> 31:57.960
the organizing committee
usually pays a hefty bonus.

31:57.960 --> 31:59.480
A certain event set up

31:59.480 --> 32:02.070
a record-breaking bonus of 25,000 euros.

32:02.310 --> 32:05.840
The organizing committee
usually chooses to buy insurance...

32:29.680 --> 32:30.440
Tang.

32:31.680 --> 32:34.400
You really impressed me today.

32:34.880 --> 32:36.590
For your level,

32:36.960 --> 32:39.400
your performance was absolutely perfect.

32:40.160 --> 32:41.680
You were just unlucky.

32:41.960 --> 32:44.240
The questions you got wrong
were extremely difficult.

32:44.240 --> 32:46.040
No one could have answered them.

32:46.110 --> 32:47.030
Besides.

32:47.590 --> 32:48.640
The next question

32:48.830 --> 32:50.680
is a teamwork question.

32:51.240 --> 32:53.030
Your team is currently in the lead,

32:53.030 --> 32:55.750
and you have the strongest teammate
backing you up.

32:55.750 --> 32:56.920
We are the ones who should be worried,

32:56.920 --> 32:57.530
not you.

33:00.380 --> 33:01.220
Duan Qiyan.

33:02.200 --> 33:04.130
You're not the one who got it wrong.

33:04.550 --> 33:05.750
I'm in a really bad mood right now.

33:05.750 --> 33:07.110
Leave me alone.

33:33.240 --> 33:34.480
Start working on

33:34.480 --> 33:35.740
the reassigned tasks.

33:38.270 --> 33:39.070
How about

33:39.510 --> 33:41.270
we find Tang Tingting first?

33:46.000 --> 33:47.660
Let her take a break to adjust.

33:47.920 --> 33:49.830
She can join us when she feels better.

33:49.830 --> 33:51.480
She is emotionally unstable right now,

33:51.480 --> 33:53.880
so she's prone
to making mistakes in a rush.

33:53.880 --> 33:55.340
If we want to win 1st place,

33:55.510 --> 33:57.040
we have no margin for error.

34:01.500 --> 34:02.560
Let's do as you say.

34:06.340 --> 34:14.719
[Women]

34:17.400 --> 34:18.400
Ms. Last In Class.

34:19.230 --> 34:22.020
You have the worst score
in the whole competition.

34:22.020 --> 34:26.770
[Women]

34:23.590 --> 34:24.730
You have nothing to lose,

34:24.730 --> 34:26.380
so why not give it your all?

34:27.150 --> 34:29.409
This isn't just about winning or losing.

34:29.480 --> 34:30.230
It's for the 2 teammates

34:30.230 --> 34:32.110
who have always trusted you.

34:33.800 --> 34:35.630
They have never given up on you.

34:36.670 --> 34:37.400
Nor have they ever

34:37.400 --> 34:39.330
treated you as just a benchwarmer.

34:40.480 --> 34:42.110
Instead, they did everything they could,

34:42.110 --> 34:43.630
trying their best to help you

34:43.630 --> 34:44.830
improve your skills.

34:45.760 --> 34:46.630
I'm here.

34:46.630 --> 34:47.360
Don't worry.

34:47.360 --> 34:48.690
Since we are teammates,

34:49.070 --> 34:50.190
we are naturally friends too.

34:50.190 --> 34:52.280
We will definitely
do very well in the exam this time,

34:52.280 --> 34:53.320
and we will definitely advance.

34:53.320 --> 34:54.070
Definitely.

34:54.070 --> 34:55.230
Cheers.

35:07.280 --> 35:08.960
It's also for your mother.

35:10.440 --> 35:11.230
I know.

35:11.880 --> 35:13.400
You must feel embarrassed

35:13.920 --> 35:15.280
because in the whole arena,

35:15.280 --> 35:16.710
only your parent came,

35:16.710 --> 35:19.170
and you even answered
the question wrongly.

35:19.760 --> 35:21.210
But do you know what I saw?

35:22.320 --> 35:23.960
I saw that in your mum's eyes,

35:24.190 --> 35:26.110
she thinks you're a great daughter—

35:26.110 --> 35:28.070
one that's able to stand in
the provincial Math Olympiad arena.

35:28.070 --> 35:29.880
There's no one else in her eyes.

35:30.760 --> 35:32.070
She was using a camera

35:32.070 --> 35:35.800
to record highlights of moments
exclusively yours the whole time.

35:41.510 --> 35:42.320
Of course.

35:43.880 --> 35:45.880
This is also fighting for yourself.

35:47.000 --> 35:48.590
Although I usually

35:48.760 --> 35:49.920
call you Ms. Last In Class

35:49.920 --> 35:51.650
and tease you from time to time,

35:52.920 --> 35:55.050
I've really been admiring you lately.

35:56.360 --> 35:58.160
Lin Zhixia's special training,

35:58.760 --> 35:59.800
that's something I can't take,

35:59.800 --> 36:01.320
yet you persevered.

36:02.230 --> 36:04.510
The effort and hardship
you put into the competition,

36:04.510 --> 36:06.310
only you know best in your heart.

36:08.630 --> 36:11.630
You have been constantly
breaking through yourself.

36:11.880 --> 36:13.150
Don't you want to see

36:13.150 --> 36:14.680
where your limit really is?

36:15.920 --> 36:18.430
[Women]

36:38.000 --> 36:38.800
Lin Zhixia.

36:39.280 --> 36:40.360
I think for the last modeling question,

36:40.360 --> 36:41.610
we can use Markov chains

36:41.610 --> 36:43.960
and binomial
and Poisson distribution models, right?

36:43.960 --> 36:44.760
I think this kind of question

36:44.760 --> 36:46.190
is most suitable to use probability rules

36:46.190 --> 36:47.390
as a modeling method.

36:47.760 --> 36:48.670
I have an idea.

36:49.030 --> 36:50.960
How about using Bayesian methods?

36:51.280 --> 36:52.400
I'm fine with anything.

36:52.400 --> 36:54.230
Jiang, what do you think?

36:56.510 --> 36:58.880
Our team has
the best average foundational ability.

36:58.880 --> 37:00.150
Our advantage is in the front end,

37:00.150 --> 37:01.460
that is, the establishment of the model

37:01.460 --> 37:03.230
and the parameter estimation stage.

37:03.230 --> 37:04.400
So Markov chains

37:04.400 --> 37:06.440
and the binomial
and Poisson distribution methods

37:06.440 --> 37:07.710
are the most secure for us.

37:07.710 --> 37:08.800
This model is classic

37:08.800 --> 37:09.960
and highly applicable.

37:09.960 --> 37:10.840
Other groups are highly likely

37:10.840 --> 37:12.670
to choose this problem-solving approach.

37:12.670 --> 37:13.630
Then what everyone is competing on

37:13.630 --> 37:15.110
is computational complexity.

37:15.110 --> 37:17.170
Our group has no absolute advantage.

37:17.400 --> 37:19.320
If Team 4 also chooses the same method,

37:19.320 --> 37:20.550
with Tang Tingting's personal ability

37:20.550 --> 37:21.590
and her condition today,

37:21.590 --> 37:23.030
she will definitely not be as good as us

37:23.030 --> 37:24.360
in terms of details and rigor.

37:24.360 --> 37:25.320
So I think

37:25.840 --> 37:27.440
Lin Zhixia won't choose this.

37:27.440 --> 37:29.840
She is too confident
in her personal abilities.

37:29.840 --> 37:31.030
So she is very likely to choose

37:31.030 --> 37:33.550
a modeling method
that emphasizes her personal thinking.

37:33.550 --> 37:36.150
Such as grey models
and Grey Relation Analysis.

37:36.150 --> 37:37.960
To widen the gap with other groups,

37:37.960 --> 37:39.710
I think it is more appropriate
to use grey models

37:39.710 --> 37:41.590
and Grey Relation Analysis now.

37:41.710 --> 37:43.320
It can show strategic insights

37:43.320 --> 37:45.280
that probability models cannot provide,

37:45.280 --> 37:47.110
and can still work

37:47.150 --> 37:48.280
when data is scarce.

37:48.670 --> 37:50.870
This method is more flexible and agile.

37:51.110 --> 37:53.510
But even if it's completed
by Lin Zhixia alone,

37:53.510 --> 37:56.190
it won't affect
their team's final presentation.

37:56.190 --> 37:57.550
What if the result is better?

37:57.550 --> 37:58.230
No.

37:59.070 --> 38:01.760
Although she has a deep understanding
of mathematical principles,

38:01.760 --> 38:03.760
she will definitely forget the fact

38:05.840 --> 38:07.590
that this is a team competition.

38:07.590 --> 38:08.550
But in this way,

38:08.590 --> 38:10.280
it relies on
your personal systems thinking

38:10.280 --> 38:11.440
and interpretation ability.

38:11.440 --> 38:13.150
Is there anything else I can do?

38:13.150 --> 38:14.590
Leave it to me, don't worry.

38:14.590 --> 38:16.190
There won't be any problems.

38:27.360 --> 38:28.190
Frankly speaking,

38:28.190 --> 38:30.880
the theoretical model
of Team 4 is very perfect,

38:31.230 --> 38:32.630
but there are 2 problems.

38:33.920 --> 38:34.710
First,

38:34.570 --> 38:37.260
[Judge]

38:34.800 --> 38:38.000
the assumptions
in the modeling process are not perfect.

38:38.000 --> 38:40.550
Of course,
the final result won't be affected,

38:40.550 --> 38:42.350
but it misses the scoring point.

38:42.800 --> 38:44.110
But if you

38:44.110 --> 38:45.030
analyze the above factors

38:45.030 --> 38:48.280
using binomial
and Poisson distributions here,

38:47.310 --> 38:49.910
[Judges]

38:48.480 --> 38:49.880
wouldn't it be better?

38:51.960 --> 38:54.320
In addition, grey models

38:54.320 --> 38:57.670
is actually a prediction model
built by fitting

38:57.670 --> 39:00.000
the original data
with an exponential function.

39:00.000 --> 39:01.110
When the data doesn't

39:01.110 --> 39:03.000
have good smoothness,

39:03.000 --> 39:04.800
it will produce certain errors.

39:04.840 --> 39:06.070
So this

39:06.070 --> 39:07.510
is very obviously

39:07.880 --> 39:10.880
a complete model thought up by one person.

39:10.960 --> 39:12.480
Which one of you is it?

39:17.070 --> 39:18.440
What this question tests

39:18.440 --> 39:20.670
is not entirely about right or wrong,

39:20.690 --> 39:22.710
[Judges]

39:20.760 --> 39:22.800
but more importantly, teamwork.

39:23.190 --> 39:24.230
A beautiful theory,

39:24.230 --> 39:26.400
combined with perfect data insight,

39:26.400 --> 39:27.710
can get a full score.

39:27.920 --> 39:30.360
I will award this contest's MVP

39:30.360 --> 39:32.400
to this student.

39:32.430 --> 39:34.550
Her model is impeccable.

39:34.670 --> 39:35.480
However,

39:35.480 --> 39:38.320
just looking at the focal point
of the last question,

39:38.320 --> 39:40.840
I think Team 2's plan

39:40.840 --> 39:42.360
is more balanced.

39:43.070 --> 39:46.150
So I want to give Team 2 full marks.

39:47.150 --> 39:48.110
Team 4...

39:49.610 --> 39:53.790
[Judges]

39:50.150 --> 39:51.150
It's 20 points.

39:53.930 --> 39:57.480
[1st Place,
Nanhai No. 1 High School Team 2]

39:56.320 --> 39:58.670
Congratulations to Team 2
for winning the contest.

39:58.670 --> 39:59.360
We won!

39:59.880 --> 40:00.480
Did we win?

40:00.710 --> 40:01.400
-We're the champions!
-Quick!

40:01.400 --> 40:02.070
We won.

40:29.740 --> 40:33.290
[1st Place,
Nanhai No. 1 High School Team 2]

40:33.290 --> 40:36.290
[2nd Place,
Nanhai No. 1 High School Team 4]

41:25.010 --> 41:25.740
You're back.

41:26.150 --> 41:28.550
Just in time.
Wash your hands and let's eat.

41:30.800 --> 41:32.590
I'm not hungry, I won't eat.

41:43.110 --> 41:44.320
This is so sumptuous.

41:45.880 --> 41:46.440
Come on.

41:46.440 --> 41:47.800
It's all your favorite.

41:48.150 --> 41:49.610
Medium rare.

41:52.230 --> 41:53.630
Double cheese.

41:54.630 --> 41:56.320
Hurry, while it's hot.

42:00.800 --> 42:01.630
Whenever we eat Western food,

42:01.630 --> 42:03.480
I always think of
how you looked when you were little.

42:03.480 --> 42:04.630
So cute.

42:05.030 --> 42:07.400
Do you remember
the first time you ate Western food?

42:07.400 --> 42:08.530
You said to me, "Mom,

42:09.150 --> 42:11.750
this is the most delicious thing
in the world."

42:12.670 --> 42:13.930
Yang from my workplace

42:14.030 --> 42:15.760
insisted on buying you snacks.

42:15.840 --> 42:17.110
When he asked what you liked,

42:17.110 --> 42:19.360
you told him you liked Western food.

42:20.150 --> 42:21.590
You wanted T-bone steak,

42:21.760 --> 42:23.220
Nasi Goreng, and borscht.

42:23.420 --> 42:25.320
You completely confused him.

42:26.280 --> 42:28.540
In the end,
he bought you to Western food.

42:36.190 --> 42:38.400
Look at me!

42:38.440 --> 42:39.280
Your dad

42:39.880 --> 42:42.000
insisted we call him before eating.

42:42.000 --> 42:43.670
He said you haven't called him for days,

42:43.670 --> 42:44.800
and he misses you.

42:45.320 --> 42:45.960
Mom.

42:47.360 --> 42:49.560
Why don't you mention the competition?

42:51.110 --> 42:52.030
Isn't it more obvious

42:52.030 --> 42:53.830
when you deliberately avoid it?

42:55.590 --> 42:57.670
I... I didn't.

42:57.670 --> 42:58.590
I know.

42:58.710 --> 43:01.360
You don't mention it
because you're afraid I'll be sad.

43:01.360 --> 43:02.710
I didn't get
a single question right today.

43:02.710 --> 43:04.070
I embarrassed you again, right?

43:04.070 --> 43:05.110
You might as well just

43:05.110 --> 43:06.840
scold me directly like before.

43:09.030 --> 43:10.550
Let's not talk about this for now.

43:10.550 --> 43:11.320
We are eating.

43:11.320 --> 43:13.450
-Fine. I apologize.
-Let’s eat first.

43:13.960 --> 43:14.840
I'm sorry.

43:16.360 --> 43:17.840
I know that by participating
in this math contest,

43:17.840 --> 43:19.570
I was just humiliating myself.

43:19.960 --> 43:21.000
I didn't want to go in the first place.

43:21.000 --> 43:22.550
You forced me to go.

43:23.150 --> 43:24.350
Have you given up now?

43:24.710 --> 43:25.920
Seeing your daughter is the dumbest one

43:25.920 --> 43:27.360
and the worst one

43:27.360 --> 43:28.920
among so many people—

43:29.000 --> 43:30.110
the one who always embarrasses you

43:30.110 --> 43:31.030
and isn't good enough—

43:31.030 --> 43:31.920
are you happy now?

43:31.920 --> 43:32.710
Tingting.

43:34.550 --> 43:35.760
Tingting. Hey...

43:37.920 --> 43:38.380
Waiter!

43:39.440 --> 43:40.210
Pack this up.

43:41.210 --> 43:42.610
Thank you. Please hurry.

43:53.510 --> 43:55.240
What's wrong with your sister?

43:57.510 --> 43:58.960
The provincial math contest.

43:58.960 --> 44:00.360
She didn't get 1st place.

44:03.000 --> 44:04.400
That's it?

44:04.400 --> 44:05.320
That scared me.

44:06.150 --> 44:08.350
Let's not talk about the contest today.

44:08.590 --> 44:09.840
If she doesn't want to eat,

44:09.840 --> 44:11.370
let her be alone for a while.

44:12.320 --> 44:12.820
Okay.

44:13.920 --> 44:15.960
Then go wash your hands and come eat.

44:32.690 --> 44:33.500
I thought

44:35.130 --> 44:36.380
being one step ahead

44:38.190 --> 44:40.590
could shield you from all the storms.

44:43.030 --> 44:44.030
Until my shadow

44:45.010 --> 44:46.810
completely blocked your light.

44:49.130 --> 44:49.940
I'm sorry.

44:50.800 --> 44:52.360
This apology

44:53.630 --> 44:56.560
cannot compare
to the height of your stacked drafts.

44:58.340 --> 44:59.670
My self-righteousness

45:00.530 --> 45:02.070
so easily shattered

45:02.900 --> 45:04.210
everyone's hard work.

45:07.670 --> 45:08.840
I don't deserve us.

45:10.670 --> 45:11.920
And I definitely don't deserve first place.
